course: dictionary
lesson: 13962
title: Words from around the world
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one country or one part of the world. Context helps you spot them. «We floated all afternoon on our lilo in the pool.» Floated and pool are clues that a lilo is something you float on in water.
explain: «Dad blew up the lilo with the pump before we went camping.» Blew up and pump show that a lilo is filled with air. It is an inflatable mattress, a plastic bed you fill with air.
explain: Lilo is a word from the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand. In America people say «air mattress» or «pool float» for the same thing. Lilo is also a girl's name, as in the film «Lilo & Stitch», so check the sentence to see which meaning is used.
explain: Safety first: offshore wind blows away from the land and can carry a lilo out to sea. Never use a lilo in the sea or in deep water without an adult.
fact: A lilo is an inflatable mattress, a plastic bed filled with air.
fact: People use a lilo for floating on water or for sleeping on when camping.
fact: «Lilo» is the word used in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: In America, people usually say «air mattress» or «pool float».
fact: Offshore wind can blow a lilo out to sea, so never use one in the sea or deep water without an adult.
exercise: «We floated all afternoon on our lilo in the pool.» What is a lilo? | A small boat with an engine | *A plastic bed filled with air, for floating on water | A type of swimming costume | A pool with a roof over it
exercise: «Dad blew up the lilo with the pump before we went camping.» Why did Dad use the pump? | To make the lilo heavier | To wash the lilo clean | *To fill the lilo with air | To cut a hole in the lilo
exercise: Ella's cousin in Chicago says, «Grab the pool float, we're going swimming.» What do Americans usually call a lilo? | A sun hat | *An air mattress | A rubber duck | A beach towel
test: In «Lilo & Stitch», what is Lilo? | A kind of wind | *A girl's name | An inflatable mattress | A swimming pool
test: Why must a child never use a lilo in the sea without an adult? | The sea is always too warm for a lilo | *Offshore wind can blow the lilo out to sea | Sea water makes the air inside disappear straight away | Lilos only work in swimming pools
exam: Sam takes his lilo to the lake, because he wants to float. What does lilo mean here? | *An inflatable mattress for floating | A girl's name | A kind of tent | A type of fish
